{
  "name": "MITICA single central beamlet, Pimazzoni benchmark configuration - profiles transcribed from MITICIInput/MITICA_geom.xlsx. Aperture cell is a CONSTANT 20 x 22 mm, as Pimazzoni et al., Fus. Eng. Des. 192 (2023) 113621 Sec. 4 specifies for the accelerator lattice; the per-grid steered aperture centres of the real machine (MITICIInput/geom/newMITICA_geom_03mmAGshift_wkerbs.h) are deliberately NOT used, because that paper's model does not include them. One aperture (Sec. 3: single-beamlet, kerb steering neglected). Geometry verified against the paper: extraction gap 6 mm, five 88 mm acceleration gaps, and bore diameters PG 14 / EG 13 / AG1 14 / AG2 14 / AG3 16 / AG4 16 / GG 16 mm. The paper's 17 mm EG exit is this taper extended to the z=32 mm face (r = 8.5 mm exactly); the spreadsheet gives the filleted form instead. Fillet radii are per corner, R = (dz^2+dr^2)/(2 dz), tangent to the adjacent segment and to the grid face; the first and last z are widened by 1 nm so a grid's end planes cannot fall outside the profile through floating-point rounding.",
